  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 IOM Iraq Displacement Tracking Matrix</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective is to provide access to up-to-date, reliable and comprehensive information about internally displaced persons (IDP) and returnee populations in Iraq, as well as their needs and vulnerabilities. This is achieved through the implementation of IOM&apos;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) tool and timely dissemination of results to government authorities, UN Humanitarian Country Team (UNHCT) partners, non-governmental organization (NGOs), think tanks, media, academics, and other stakeholders. The project will be implemented across Iraq and have the following key outputs: a. To increase access to displacement information through the distribution of DTM products; b. To enhance regional and national government authorities&apos; data management capacities; and c. To improve access to data for relevant partners.</narrative>
  </description>
